WEBVTT

1
00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.708
- Nicholas bell.
- Mr. Campano.

2
00:00:23.732 --> 00:00:25.067
In person.

3
00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:27.444
You're my hero.

4
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.130
Just doing my job.

5
00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:30.465
Sure.

6
00:00:30.489 --> 00:00:33.968
But I'm guessing if my associate.
Mr. Grey. drew any other public defender.

7
00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:35.577
he'd be sitting in jail right now.

8
00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.038
That may be true.

9
00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:40.266
Cigar?

10
00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.351
Before lunch?

11
00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:45.462
There's no such thing as
a bad time for a good cigar.

12
00:00:47.798 --> 00:00:48.882
Save it for later.

13
00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:52.195
Consider it a signing bonus.

14
00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:54.030
I haven't signed anything.

15
00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.264
- Have I?
- Not yet.

16
00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:02.372
So. tell me. why are you leaving
the public defender's office?

17
00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:04.313
I haven't decided to leave yet.

18
00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:06.251
But I just had another kid.

19
00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:07.484
That's what I figured.

20
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:10.821
Is this a job offer?

21
00:01:11.864 --> 00:01:12.966
No.

22
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.717
But I understand you have one

23
00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:18.596
from a prestigious. white-shoe
criminal defense firm in Houston.

24
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.683
Those are all the clients you'll
be expected to defend there.

25
00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:24.144
Corporations destroying
the environment.

26
00:01:24.168 --> 00:01:26.229
banks stealing from retirement funds

27
00:01:26.253 --> 00:01:28.439
and a whole cadre of rich sociopaths

28
00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:31.800
facing charges for everything
from extortion to murder.

29
00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:34.303
I'll pay you double.

30
00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.782
You can stay here in Austin.

31
00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:39.600
I'll just be a…

32
00:01:40.726 --> 00:01:42.060
Another client.

33
00:01:47.566 --> 00:01:50.152
If you're going to work
for criminals. Mr. Bell.

34
00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:53.030
you might as well work
for the generous ones.

35
00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:01.598
Pick your poison.

36
00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.267
Don't have anything stronger?

37
00:02:04.291 --> 00:02:08.127
Not for 75-year-olds with heart conditions
who've just come back from the dead.

38
00:02:11.048 --> 00:02:12.466
It's got a lot of sugar.

39
00:02:13.342 --> 00:02:15.111
Might wanna take it easy.

40
00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.012
I'm gonna toss you right off this plane.

41
00:02:19.014 --> 00:02:21.225
Just when I was starting to get used to it.

42
00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.578
Yeah. that's the problem.

43
00:02:23.602 --> 00:02:24.853
Getting used to it.

44
00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:27.064
Makes it hard to stop.

45
00:02:28.315 --> 00:02:29.584
This wasn't your fault.

46
00:02:29.608 --> 00:02:31.568
What if I'd said no to frank?

47
00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:34.238
Kept flying coach.

48
00:02:36.615 --> 00:02:38.134
Maybe things would've been different.

49
00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.243
Maybe.

50
00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:42.204
I need to make this right.

51
00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.830
I owe that to you.

52
00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:45.707
To all of you.

53
00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:47.918
Then we will.

54
00:04:12.169 --> 00:04:14.564
Why on earth would they go to Paris?

55
00:04:14.588 --> 00:04:16.608
We don't even know
where to meet them.

56
00:04:16.632 --> 00:04:18.902
Then we'll have to wait till they tell us.

57
00:04:18.926 --> 00:04:20.344
That's not very fun. is it?

58
00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:25.098
You're not worried?

59
00:04:25.724 --> 00:04:26.868
I am.

60
00:04:26.892 --> 00:04:29.537
But at the moment. we're
traveling with five million dollars

61
00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:32.790
Teddy camp a no owes to
an international drug cartel.

62
00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:34.733
so it's not at the very top of my list.

63
00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.464
Look. I'm concerned
about Bailey too. of course.

64
00:04:39.488 --> 00:04:40.948
But I trust Nicholas.

65
00:04:41.907 --> 00:04:42.967
You do?

66
00:04:42.991 --> 00:04:45.220
Yeah. he loves Bailey
as much as you do.

67
00:04:45.244 --> 00:04:46.804
You see eye-to-eye on that.

68
00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:49.224
He'd never put her in harm's way.

69
00:04:49.248 --> 00:04:51.250
And he could be helpful with frank.

70
00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:54.586
Well. that part might be complicated.

71
00:04:55.254 --> 00:04:56.922
You mean if Quinn's involved?

72
00:04:57.798 --> 00:05:00.610
Teddy's always been
rash. but Quinn's smart.

73
00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:02.469
Frank adores her.

74
00:05:03.637 --> 00:05:05.138
If Quinn's involved…

75
00:05:06.598 --> 00:05:07.599
Yeah.

76
00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:09.994
So a question. Ms. Favreau.

77
00:05:10.018 --> 00:05:11.079
Why France?

78
00:05:11.103 --> 00:05:13.438
Why not London. the
financial capital of Europe?

79
00:05:14.648 --> 00:05:18.777
It was time for my business to expand.

80
00:05:19.695 --> 00:05:24.074
And it felt like the perfect
way to honor my mother.

81
00:05:24.867 --> 00:05:26.052
Is she from Paris?

82
00:05:26.076 --> 00:05:29.973
No. but she was from èze. on the coast.

83
00:05:29.997 --> 00:05:32.475
And as there no banks
available to buy there…

84
00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:34.960
No. they deal more in perfumes.

85
00:05:40.257 --> 00:05:42.485
How the fuck do you
lose five million dollars?

86
00:05:42.509 --> 00:05:43.802
Did I fucking say I lost it?

87
00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:46.739
Whoever switched the RFID
on the can must've taken it...

88
00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:48.658
I don't wanna know. I don't wanna know.

89
00:05:48.682 --> 00:05:50.451
- Right. Saint Quinn.
- Fuck you.

90
00:05:50.475 --> 00:05:52.829
If the syndicate doesn't get their
money they're gonna come after all of us.

91
00:05:52.853 --> 00:05:54.330
What do you want from me. Teddy?

92
00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:55.814
Well. right now. I could use a loan.

93
00:05:56.648 --> 00:05:58.042
I don't have that kinda cash.

94
00:05:58.066 --> 00:06:00.503
- You own a bank.
- Yeah. which has to stay legitimate.

95
00:06:00.527 --> 00:06:02.130
So where the fuck am I gonna
come up with this money?

96
00:06:02.154 --> 00:06:04.323
- Talk to dad?
- He'll lose his shit.

97
00:06:04.865 --> 00:06:06.116
He has the money.

98
00:06:06.617 --> 00:06:08.261
It's better he hears it from you.

99
00:06:08.285 --> 00:06:09.703
You gonna rat me out?

100
00:06:10.245 --> 00:06:11.246
Not me.

101
00:06:11.788 --> 00:06:13.892
I assume the syndicate
decided to work with you

102
00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:15.477
because they thought
you had dad's backing.

103
00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:18.170
So. if you are not holding
up your side of the deal…

104
00:06:20.714 --> 00:06:22.257
Quinnie. he'll kill me.

105
00:06:22.841 --> 00:06:24.801
He's pretty used to
your fuck ups at this point.

106
00:06:27.054 --> 00:06:28.889
I have to get back to my interview.

107
00:06:29.473 --> 00:06:30.724
Just talk to dad.

108
00:06:31.308 --> 00:06:33.477
Please try not to screw up again. okay?

109
00:06:47.282 --> 00:06:49.677
Not exactly how I
thought I'd first see Paris.

110
00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:51.703
Pretty spectacular though?

111
00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.582
Your grandmother.
she preferred Tuscany.

112
00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:57.626
Where her family was from.

113
00:06:58.168 --> 00:06:59.687
I was always drawn here.

114
00:06:59.711 --> 00:07:01.380
I'd drag your mother to the louvre.

115
00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.882
Just trying to give her what I never had.

116
00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:06.468
She humored me.

117
00:07:07.052 --> 00:07:09.012
She never loved Paris the way I did.

118
00:07:10.681 --> 00:07:11.741
But your father…

119
00:07:11.765 --> 00:07:14.202
He took Hannah here
for their honeymoon.

120
00:07:14.226 --> 00:07:15.537
She told me.

121
00:07:15.561 --> 00:07:16.788
The Victoria palace.

122
00:07:16.812 --> 00:07:19.123
The best hotel in the world.

123
00:07:20.232 --> 00:07:22.335
And small. discreet.

124
00:07:22.359 --> 00:07:23.419
Only 60 keys.

125
00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.338
That's where we're staying?

126
00:07:25.362 --> 00:07:27.197
Figured it'd be an easy rendezvous.

127
00:07:29.408 --> 00:07:30.450
Also. frank.

128
00:07:30.951 --> 00:07:33.638
he likes to stay at hôtel lumineux.

129
00:07:33.662 --> 00:07:36.081
the hoity-toity five-star down the street.

130
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.144
You're gonna wait. right?

131
00:07:39.168 --> 00:07:42.129
You're not gonna approach him
until we've discussed it with Hannah.

132
00:07:42.629 --> 00:07:44.440
Not directly. no.

133
00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:46.466
No. he doesn't love surprises.

134
00:07:46.967 --> 00:07:48.218
Neither do we.

135
00:08:10.782 --> 00:08:12.719
Waiting to greet me.

136
00:08:12.743 --> 00:08:13.970
I feel like royalty.

137
00:08:13.994 --> 00:08:15.370
I'm just happy we're all here.

138
00:08:17.331 --> 00:08:18.790
Yeah. okay. okay.

139
00:08:19.791 --> 00:08:21.793
I'm turning 80. I'm not dying.

140
00:08:22.503 --> 00:08:23.754
At least not yet.

141
00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:37.869
Quinnie here?

142
00:08:37.893 --> 00:08:40.413
She's just finishing up an interview
with some fancy business rag.

143
00:08:40.437 --> 00:08:43.374
Which is just as well. We can chat.

144
00:08:43.398 --> 00:08:44.598
Why? Is there something wrong?

145
00:08:45.067 --> 00:08:46.944
No. just a few things to discuss.

146
00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:49.797
I have some fresh behikes.

147
00:08:49.821 --> 00:08:50.965
Come on. pop.

148
00:08:50.989 --> 00:08:53.408
You know I can't do your
weird morning cigar thing.

149
00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:57.263
Shit. I gotta take this.

150
00:08:57.287 --> 00:08:58.330
I'll be right back.

151
00:08:59.164 --> 00:09:01.059
- Hello?
- Mr. Campano.

152
00:09:01.083 --> 00:09:03.561
One of our friends at
the Marseille train station.

153
00:09:03.585 --> 00:09:05.879
ID'd a couple on the 7:01 to Paris.

154
00:09:06.463 --> 00:09:07.506
You're sure it's them?

155
00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.341
He seemed fairly certain.

156
00:09:10.259 --> 00:09:11.969
When does the train get there?

157
00:09:12.553 --> 00:09:15.597
On time arrival at gare de
Lyon 30 minutes from now.

158
00:09:17.391 --> 00:09:18.892
Text me the info.

159
00:09:21.353 --> 00:09:23.397
I need men at the gare de Lyon. now.

160
00:09:27.359 --> 00:09:29.087
It could be worse. We're in Paris.

161
00:09:29.111 --> 00:09:31.113
- It's almost romantic.
- Almost.

162
00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:33.991
Hang on. My phone.

163
00:09:39.079 --> 00:09:41.599
I can think of worse places to hide out.

164
00:09:41.623 --> 00:09:42.624
Wait.

165
00:09:43.876 --> 00:09:46.187
They'll have men all over
the station looking for us.

166
00:09:46.211 --> 00:09:47.212
Let's find some cover.

167
00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.676
We have eight-year-old twins.
but I remember those days.

168
00:09:53.969 --> 00:09:55.429
Here. let us help you out.

169
00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:57.991
- Thank you.
- Yes.

170
00:09:58.015 --> 00:09:59.016
Merci.

171
00:10:00.726 --> 00:10:02.019
Hey.

172
00:10:02.769 --> 00:10:03.770
Merci.

173
00:10:17.201 --> 00:10:18.845
Are we sure they were on the train?

174
00:10:18.869 --> 00:10:20.495
That's what we were told…

175
00:10:28.629 --> 00:10:29.671
Wait. I think I see them.

176
00:10:40.766 --> 00:10:44.621
How did you miss them?

177
00:10:44.645 --> 00:10:46.247
No. I don't give a shit how you do it.

178
00:10:46.271 --> 00:10:47.523
I need you to find them!

179
00:10:50.108 --> 00:10:51.294
Hi. dad.

180
00:10:51.318 --> 00:10:53.004
Quinnie.

181
00:10:53.028 --> 00:10:54.088
Hi.

182
00:10:54.112 --> 00:10:55.381
How's my girl?

183
00:10:55.405 --> 00:10:57.300
- I'm good.
- Yeah?

184
00:10:57.324 --> 00:11:00.386
Busy with the acquisition.
but I'm glad you came.

185
00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:01.471
Are you sure about that?

186
00:11:01.495 --> 00:11:02.639
Yes.

187
00:11:02.663 --> 00:11:05.249
It's gonna be nice. the three
of us celebrating your birthday.

188
00:11:06.667 --> 00:11:08.895
Any idea what's going on there?

189
00:11:08.919 --> 00:11:12.256
You know Teddy. always
lighting fires for himself to put out.

190
00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:14.484
Yeah.

191
00:11:14.508 --> 00:11:16.236
Shoot. Sorry. I need to take this.

192
00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:18.071
- I'll catch up with you later?
- All right.

193
00:11:18.095 --> 00:11:19.096
Love you.

194
00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:04.308
Welcome. Mr. Bell.

195
00:12:05.642 --> 00:12:07.453
We have the room you requested.

196
00:12:07.477 --> 00:12:08.478
Can I take you to it?

197
00:12:13.609 --> 00:12:15.944
Why don't you let Ms.
Gachon show you the room?

198
00:12:42.846 --> 00:12:44.365
How about Paris?

199
00:12:44.389 --> 00:12:45.807
We can all go.

200
00:12:48.769 --> 00:12:50.538
You have not lived

201
00:12:50.562 --> 00:12:54.483
until you've smoked a cigar in
the lounge at the hôtel lumineux.

202
00:12:55.067 --> 00:12:56.151
Is that right?

203
00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:58.922
We can take the kids
for a hot chocolate tasting.

204
00:12:58.946 --> 00:13:00.280
Jenny loves that.

205
00:13:01.114 --> 00:13:02.115
Loved that.

206
00:13:05.369 --> 00:13:06.804
You need another drink.

207
00:13:06.828 --> 00:13:08.747
What a fucking month!

208
00:13:10.666 --> 00:13:14.437
First Jenny. now this New York bullshit.

209
00:13:14.461 --> 00:13:15.980
They're ticky-tack charges.

210
00:13:16.004 --> 00:13:17.065
Bobby can handle it.

211
00:13:17.089 --> 00:13:19.258
Bobby looks good in a sharkskin suit.

212
00:13:21.093 --> 00:13:22.737
But he's no Nicky bell.

213
00:13:22.761 --> 00:13:24.513
I won't do what Bobby does.

214
00:13:25.389 --> 00:13:27.641
I'm of no use to you if I get disbarred.

215
00:13:28.517 --> 00:13:29.977
I won't cross that line.

216
00:13:31.895 --> 00:13:33.313
Who's asking you to?

217
00:13:52.708 --> 00:13:54.227
Nicholas.

218
00:13:54.251 --> 00:13:55.586
Thank god.

219
00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:57.588
Where's Bailey?

220
00:13:58.797 --> 00:14:00.257
- Hi.
- Hi.

221
00:14:01.842 --> 00:14:02.843
Bails.

222
00:14:03.343 --> 00:14:04.803
Hey. dad.

223
00:14:05.345 --> 00:14:07.365
- It's not safe for...
- It's not safe for me to be here.

224
00:14:07.389 --> 00:14:08.449
Yes. I know.

225
00:14:08.473 --> 00:14:10.660
Well. for either of you. What's going on?

226
00:14:10.684 --> 00:14:11.935
Why are you here?

227
00:14:12.936 --> 00:14:14.938
Maybe we should all sit down.

228
00:14:20.444 --> 00:14:23.947
I went through this
after Kate died. but I…

229
00:14:25.157 --> 00:14:27.385
I knew Ivan was a friend. but I…

230
00:14:27.409 --> 00:14:29.679
But you didn't know he'd
become a prosecutor.

231
00:14:29.703 --> 00:14:31.973
- I should've listened to her.
- You and me both.

232
00:14:31.997 --> 00:14:33.558
I just… I couldn't hear it.

233
00:14:33.582 --> 00:14:34.833
And I couldn't…

234
00:14:36.668 --> 00:14:39.838
I just couldn't hold back. I
couldn't pull away from frank.

235
00:14:40.756 --> 00:14:46.386
My mom knew that. and so she decided
to take matters into her own hands.

236
00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:49.574
And you think they killed her.

237
00:14:49.598 --> 00:14:52.327
All the privileged
information I had in my files.

238
00:14:52.351 --> 00:14:54.770
if the feds had been able
to get at that through Kate.

239
00:14:55.354 --> 00:14:57.856
it could've toppled the
campanos' entire organization.

240
00:14:59.066 --> 00:15:00.668
So frank did do this.

241
00:15:00.692 --> 00:15:01.836
No.

242
00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:03.362
No. he wouldn't have.

243
00:15:04.446 --> 00:15:05.781
No. I'm sure of it.

244
00:15:06.323 --> 00:15:07.533
Teddy.

245
00:15:11.787 --> 00:15:14.665
Yes. I know you've been very generous.

246
00:15:16.124 --> 00:15:17.668
Yes. I know…

247
00:15:18.585 --> 00:15:22.381
But I can make a partial delivery…

248
00:15:23.757 --> 00:15:25.735
I understand that's not what
Mr. Perec and I agreed to.

249
00:15:25.759 --> 00:15:26.959
but if I could speak with him…

250
00:15:27.928 --> 00:15:30.281
look. I'm gonna get
you your fucking money.

251
00:15:30.305 --> 00:15:32.224
I just need a minute. okay?

252
00:15:55.163 --> 00:15:57.308
Are you still into valium
or have you moved on

253
00:15:57.332 --> 00:15:58.560
to something stronger?

254
00:15:58.584 --> 00:16:00.145
It's just ativan. but
thanks for the concern.

255
00:16:00.169 --> 00:16:01.896
What are you doing?

256
00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.481
Leave me alone. I've got it handled.

257
00:16:03.505 --> 00:16:04.858
It doesn't seem like it.

258
00:16:04.882 --> 00:16:07.009
You wanna take over?
You wanna run the show?

259
00:16:07.926 --> 00:16:09.571
I am just trying to help.

260
00:16:09.595 --> 00:16:11.739
You wanna be helpful.
find me a fucking loan.

261
00:16:11.763 --> 00:16:12.848
I did.

262
00:16:15.058 --> 00:16:16.602
Just talk to him.

263
00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:29.865
Hey.

264
00:16:35.579 --> 00:16:36.580
Are you okay?

265
00:16:41.293 --> 00:16:44.505
If I'd only walked away when I
realized what Nicholas was doing…

266
00:16:46.423 --> 00:16:48.091
Kate told me. I…

267
00:16:49.343 --> 00:16:50.677
I just argued.

268
00:16:52.554 --> 00:16:53.615
This is my fault.

269
00:16:53.639 --> 00:16:55.742
- You were young.
- Yeah.

270
00:16:55.766 --> 00:16:58.161
And Nicholas was larger than life.

271
00:16:58.185 --> 00:17:00.521
It was an impossible situation.

272
00:17:01.188 --> 00:17:02.582
I don't know what I would've done.

273
00:17:02.606 --> 00:17:05.334
But I certainly don't
think anyone is to blame.

274
00:17:05.358 --> 00:17:08.362
Or at least. not anyone here.

275
00:17:09.946 --> 00:17:10.948
That's generous.

276
00:17:12.866 --> 00:17:14.117
I love you.

277
00:17:35.931 --> 00:17:37.391
Hey. Hey. hey. hey.

278
00:17:38.225 --> 00:17:40.185
I'm trying to work my
way up to an apology here.

279
00:17:41.019 --> 00:17:42.312
To my dad?

280
00:17:42.938 --> 00:17:45.732
Your dad. you. Charlie.

281
00:17:46.233 --> 00:17:47.359
It's a long list.

282
00:17:56.577 --> 00:17:57.995
I don't deserve you.

283
00:17:59.621 --> 00:18:00.622
Probably not.

284
00:18:05.836 --> 00:18:07.462
- We got a plan.
- Yeah.

285
00:18:08.172 --> 00:18:09.298
So do we.

286
00:18:12.426 --> 00:18:14.011
I thought they were shipping drugs.

287
00:18:14.595 --> 00:18:17.514
We think maybe Teddy's not
shipping drugs for the syndicate.

288
00:18:18.098 --> 00:18:19.576
We think he's laundering their money.

289
00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:21.119
The money could be a bargaining chip.

290
00:18:21.143 --> 00:18:22.829
We could make a deal for all of us.

291
00:18:22.853 --> 00:18:25.290
We wanna go directly
to Teddy and Quinn.

292
00:18:25.314 --> 00:18:26.315
Quinn?

293
00:18:27.691 --> 00:18:29.669
We think Quinn might be involved.

294
00:18:29.693 --> 00:18:32.779
She was Teddy's first phone
call when the money went missing.

295
00:18:33.488 --> 00:18:35.258
So she was lying to us?

296
00:18:35.282 --> 00:18:36.676
She was lying to me?

297
00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:38.285
Well. it sounded complicated.

298
00:18:39.286 --> 00:18:41.598
She seemed so sincere when
she was talking about my mom.

299
00:18:41.622 --> 00:18:43.266
Well. she was close with Kate.

300
00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:44.666
She wasn't lying about that.

301
00:18:45.375 --> 00:18:48.354
It's not the worst thing
if Quinn is involved.

302
00:18:48.378 --> 00:18:50.148
She's more rational than Teddy.

303
00:18:50.172 --> 00:18:51.274
That's not saying much.

304
00:18:51.298 --> 00:18:54.694
And even if she makes a deal. Teddy'll
break it as soon as he's in the clear.

305
00:18:54.718 --> 00:18:56.112
She won't be able to stop that.

306
00:18:56.136 --> 00:18:58.531
So you. you still wanna go to frank.

307
00:18:58.555 --> 00:19:01.701
Well. frank has been listening
to my counsel for 40 years.

308
00:19:01.725 --> 00:19:04.478
Going to frank with what we know now.

309
00:19:04.978 --> 00:19:07.189
I might get to the truth
of what happened to Kate.

310
00:19:07.731 --> 00:19:11.235
And that's the closest we're
ever gonna get to justice for her.

311
00:19:11.735 --> 00:19:14.154
Are you willing to let
that go? Either of you?

312
00:19:15.155 --> 00:19:16.740
After Kate died…

313
00:19:18.283 --> 00:19:21.954
I was obsessed with
getting justice for her.

314
00:19:24.373 --> 00:19:25.457
But now.

315
00:19:27.251 --> 00:19:30.671
the important thing is us being together.

316
00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:37.636
I wanna know what happened
to her. more than anything.

317
00:19:38.554 --> 00:19:41.431
I've been living with half-truths
about her my whole life.

318
00:19:42.015 --> 00:19:44.935
I think our safety has to be the priority.

319
00:19:47.354 --> 00:19:50.607
And if there's a chance
we can all be together.

320
00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:55.821
Okay.

321
00:19:57.197 --> 00:19:59.133
Okay. we do it your way.

322
00:19:59.157 --> 00:20:00.844
What's the plan?

323
00:20:00.868 --> 00:20:03.203
How are you gonna
get to Quinn and Teddy?

324
00:20:10.919 --> 00:20:12.397
Hell. it's noon somewhere.

325
00:20:12.421 --> 00:20:13.755
That's more like it.

326
00:20:14.423 --> 00:20:15.424
I've got one.

327
00:20:18.051 --> 00:20:21.239
"At college. study well
and be like a cleanser.

328
00:20:21.263 --> 00:20:23.682
Work fast and leave no rings."

329
00:20:25.309 --> 00:20:27.603
Did I give that to you?

330
00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:30.105
- That's awful.
- Really?

331
00:20:30.981 --> 00:20:32.733
I always thought it was good advice.

332
00:20:34.902 --> 00:20:37.905
Speaking of which. I could use some…

333
00:20:46.622 --> 00:20:47.873
Sorry. pop.

334
00:20:48.457 --> 00:20:50.143
I'm gonna have to take a rain check.

335
00:20:50.167 --> 00:20:51.668
We'll smoke them later. yeah?

336
00:20:52.377 --> 00:20:53.587
Sure.

337
00:21:09.353 --> 00:21:10.521
Did he talk to you?

338
00:21:12.523 --> 00:21:13.524
No.

339
00:21:16.193 --> 00:21:19.404
I'm gonna have to step in
before he gets us all killed.

340
00:21:19.905 --> 00:21:22.491
If you do that he'll lose
the respect of the syndicate.

341
00:21:24.034 --> 00:21:27.079
Maybe it's time to put
someone else in charge.

342
00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:31.750
You know I don't want that.

343
00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:35.504
And I've never wanted it for you.

344
00:21:39.174 --> 00:21:41.093
But we're running out of options.

345
00:21:55.607 --> 00:21:56.900
It's a lot?

346
00:21:59.611 --> 00:22:00.612
Yeah.

347
00:22:01.613 --> 00:22:03.866
But at least it all makes sense now.

348
00:22:05.868 --> 00:22:07.512
And she wasn't just a victim.

349
00:22:07.536 --> 00:22:12.374
She was brave and strong
and trying to protect her family.

350
00:22:12.916 --> 00:22:14.376
Just like her daughter.

351
00:22:17.963 --> 00:22:19.315
I'm sorry.

352
00:22:19.339 --> 00:22:20.924
You are? For what?

353
00:22:22.843 --> 00:22:24.904
I was so skeptical of
what you guys were doing.

354
00:22:24.928 --> 00:22:27.806
I… I feel bad that I doubted you and dad.

355
00:22:28.765 --> 00:22:29.826
Well. you should.

356
00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:32.519
Who ever heard of a
20-something doubting their parents?

357
00:22:36.023 --> 00:22:38.317
Bails? What is it?

358
00:22:38.942 --> 00:22:40.068
You having second thoughts?

359
00:22:40.986 --> 00:22:41.987
No.

360
00:22:43.280 --> 00:22:45.216
Just be careful.

361
00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:46.467
- Yeah.
- Okay?

362
00:22:46.491 --> 00:22:47.552
Both of you.

363
00:22:47.576 --> 00:22:48.636
We will.

364
00:22:48.660 --> 00:22:49.912
Okay. Promise.

365
00:22:51.496 --> 00:22:53.040
Keep an eye on him.

366
00:22:53.582 --> 00:22:54.851
Use the burner if you need us.

367
00:22:54.875 --> 00:22:56.126
Okay.

368
00:23:08.764 --> 00:23:09.806
Daddy.

369
00:23:11.141 --> 00:23:12.226
Daddy.

370
00:23:15.729 --> 00:23:17.648
- Daddy.
- Yes. Katie?

371
00:23:18.565 --> 00:23:20.192
Don't you want some hot chocolate?

372
00:23:20.692 --> 00:23:22.212
Bring me some back.

373
00:23:22.236 --> 00:23:24.339
Tell quinnie to bring me one too.

374
00:23:24.363 --> 00:23:26.508
Katie. I love you all the world.

375
00:23:26.532 --> 00:23:27.950
I love you too.

376
00:23:31.745 --> 00:23:33.747
I told it would be a celebration.

377
00:23:34.957 --> 00:23:36.226
I should've gotten you off.

378
00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:37.852
You're being too hard on yourself.

379
00:23:37.876 --> 00:23:39.729
It's only six months.

380
00:23:39.753 --> 00:23:41.380
That's a win for the good guys.

381
00:23:42.714 --> 00:23:44.776
When I get out. we'll
come back here for longer.

382
00:23:44.800 --> 00:23:46.361
And we'll go to èze.

383
00:23:46.385 --> 00:23:48.029
It's on the riviera.

384
00:23:48.053 --> 00:23:50.430
There's a hike there the
octogenarians swear by.

385
00:23:51.348 --> 00:23:52.700
You think we'll make it to 80?

386
00:23:52.724 --> 00:23:53.785
That's my point.

387
00:23:53.809 --> 00:23:54.911
They walk it every day.

388
00:23:54.935 --> 00:23:56.871
They swear it keeps them young.

389
00:23:56.895 --> 00:23:58.814
It's called Nietzsche's path.

390
00:23:59.606 --> 00:24:00.858
Very French.

391
00:24:06.238 --> 00:24:08.365
I'm going to need someone
to visit me in prison.

392
00:24:10.242 --> 00:24:12.220
I'm going to need to get information.

393
00:24:12.244 --> 00:24:14.997
I'm going to need to
pass along certain orders.

394
00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:19.352
You should ask Lane to do that.

395
00:24:19.376 --> 00:24:22.754
If Lane comes. every FBI
agent in Texas will be listening in.

396
00:24:26.383 --> 00:24:27.384
But if it's you…

397
00:24:31.221 --> 00:24:33.682
Abusing attorney client
privilege is against the law.

398
00:24:34.349 --> 00:24:35.434
You know that.

399
00:24:36.101 --> 00:24:39.438
I know I need to keep
control of my organization.

400
00:24:43.400 --> 00:24:45.044
You've never asked me for this.

401
00:24:45.068 --> 00:24:49.323
No. I hardly ever ask anyone to
cross that line for me personally.

402
00:24:50.407 --> 00:24:52.993
It requires a deep level of trust.

403
00:24:55.329 --> 00:24:56.330
I'm flattered.

404
00:24:57.748 --> 00:24:58.916
You should be.

405
00:25:01.001 --> 00:25:06.256
Nietzsche said what is done for love
always occurs beyond good and evil.

406
00:26:05.482 --> 00:26:06.483
You stay here.

407
00:26:07.609 --> 00:26:09.069
I want you on Bailey.

408
00:26:35.053 --> 00:26:36.281
I see him.

409
00:26:36.305 --> 00:26:38.575
He's outside the watch store.
He has two guards with him.

410
00:26:38.599 --> 00:26:39.659
Copy.

411
00:26:39.683 --> 00:26:41.727
Let me see what I can do about that.

412
00:26:54.615 --> 00:26:55.782
Stay out here.

413
00:26:59.286 --> 00:27:01.639
He went inside. Sweating.

414
00:27:01.663 --> 00:27:02.789
Good.

415
00:27:03.540 --> 00:27:05.310
Yeah. but the guards are still there.

416
00:27:05.334 --> 00:27:06.793
We need to get him alone.

417
00:27:07.836 --> 00:27:09.898
Another coffee. ma'am?

418
00:27:09.922 --> 00:27:10.964
Yes. thank you.

419
00:27:12.257 --> 00:27:13.675
- Bonjour. madame.
- Merci.

420
00:27:20.682 --> 00:27:22.243
What are we looking for today?

421
00:27:22.267 --> 00:27:24.037
I don't know…

422
00:27:24.061 --> 00:27:28.958
let me see something large. masculine…
what someone older would wear.

423
00:27:28.982 --> 00:27:31.503
Of course! Would you
like some tea? A coffee?

424
00:27:31.527 --> 00:27:32.629
No. no… just the watch.

425
00:27:32.653 --> 00:27:33.755
A glass of champagne. perhaps?

426
00:27:33.779 --> 00:27:35.948
No. no… actually. yeah. Thanks.

427
00:27:44.081 --> 00:27:45.600
You following me?

428
00:27:45.624 --> 00:27:46.917
More like babysitting.

429
00:27:48.585 --> 00:27:52.690
Don't think buying a $50.000
watch makes up for losing five million.

430
00:27:52.714 --> 00:27:54.442
It's a present for dad.

431
00:27:54.466 --> 00:27:56.528
If you live long enough to give it to him.

432
00:27:56.552 --> 00:27:57.612
What are you doing here?

433
00:27:57.636 --> 00:27:59.030
Taking over.

434
00:27:59.054 --> 00:28:00.055
Temporarily.

435
00:28:01.098 --> 00:28:04.244
Fixing your mess so it doesn't
lead to something more permanent.

436
00:28:04.268 --> 00:28:05.328
You talked to dad?

437
00:28:05.352 --> 00:28:06.704
Damn right I talked to dad.

438
00:28:06.728 --> 00:28:07.831
I told you this was my thing.

439
00:28:07.855 --> 00:28:09.707
- I told you I didn't want dad involved.
- I know.

440
00:28:09.731 --> 00:28:11.835
But I couldn't watch
you self-destruct again.

441
00:28:11.859 --> 00:28:13.419
Your champagne. sir.

442
00:28:13.443 --> 00:28:15.028
He'll need one too.

443
00:28:20.200 --> 00:28:21.577
Is he still inside?

444
00:28:22.077 --> 00:28:23.346
Yeah.

445
00:28:23.370 --> 00:28:25.598
Why would he ignore perec?

446
00:28:25.622 --> 00:28:27.249
You think he has any idea?

447
00:28:27.833 --> 00:28:29.269
Maybe you should get out of there.

448
00:28:29.293 --> 00:28:31.354
We agreed this is our best play.

449
00:28:31.378 --> 00:28:33.731
Sure. but… if he's made you…

450
00:28:33.755 --> 00:28:35.733
Well. then what? We
still have his money.

451
00:28:35.757 --> 00:28:37.068
I think he's just afraid.

452
00:28:37.092 --> 00:28:38.278
Just send him another text.

453
00:28:38.302 --> 00:28:40.155
See if you can speed him along.

454
00:28:40.179 --> 00:28:42.490
No. I don't like it.

455
00:28:42.514 --> 00:28:45.100
Well. you don't have to like
it. You just have to trust me.

456
00:28:54.234 --> 00:28:55.569
Your champagne.

457
00:28:58.906 --> 00:29:01.867
- I'll have another.
- Yes. sir. One moment please.

458
00:29:02.659 --> 00:29:04.036
So. dad gave you the money?

459
00:29:04.661 --> 00:29:07.348
Of course not. He's livid. He's
not gonna give you that kinda cash.

460
00:29:07.372 --> 00:29:08.474
How the fuck does that help me?

461
00:29:08.498 --> 00:29:09.642
He spoke with perec.

462
00:29:09.666 --> 00:29:11.168
He said he smoothed things over.

463
00:29:12.085 --> 00:29:13.730
You don't smooth things
over with these people.

464
00:29:13.754 --> 00:29:14.814
That's not how it works.

465
00:29:14.838 --> 00:29:16.566
He's been doing this a
lot longer than you have.

466
00:29:16.590 --> 00:29:18.485
- I think he knows how it works.
- You're wrong.

467
00:29:18.509 --> 00:29:19.819
Dad was never in this league.

468
00:29:19.843 --> 00:29:23.364
And unless you can magically
make five million dollars appear

469
00:29:23.388 --> 00:29:26.558
by end of day. we're all fucked.

470
00:29:31.188 --> 00:29:33.023
He's watching you?

471
00:29:33.607 --> 00:29:35.126
That doesn't make any sense.

472
00:29:35.150 --> 00:29:37.069
I was there when dad spoke to him.

473
00:29:37.569 --> 00:29:39.029
It sounded like…

474
00:29:50.207 --> 00:29:53.168
Yeah. I changed my mind.
We're not gonna be buying.

475
00:29:54.086 --> 00:29:55.671
Dad would love that one.

476
00:29:57.881 --> 00:29:59.132
Buy the watch.

477
00:29:59.716 --> 00:30:01.528
Go back to the hotel.

478
00:30:01.552 --> 00:30:03.446
Quinn. you don't know these people.

479
00:30:03.470 --> 00:30:05.138
Actually. I do.

480
00:30:11.854 --> 00:30:12.855
Anything?

481
00:30:15.107 --> 00:30:16.108
Let's go.

482
00:30:16.692 --> 00:30:18.419
Yeah. he's leaving.

483
00:30:18.443 --> 00:30:20.696
Looks like he's going
back the way he came.

484
00:30:21.363 --> 00:30:22.990
Do you think I should follow?

485
00:30:27.661 --> 00:30:28.912
Let's take a walk.

486
00:30:48.473 --> 00:30:49.600
Housekeeping.

487
00:30:50.309 --> 00:30:53.520
- Could you come back later. please?
- No problem.

488
00:30:54.438 --> 00:30:55.439
Grandpa?

489
00:30:58.525 --> 00:30:59.693
Grandpa?

490
00:31:08.368 --> 00:31:09.929
Where is he?

491
00:31:09.953 --> 00:31:11.264
I don't know.

492
00:31:11.288 --> 00:31:12.539
He didn't say.

493
00:32:05.717 --> 00:32:07.469
- To Nietzsche.
- To Nietzsche.

494
00:32:13.016 --> 00:32:14.351
Wait until we get to èze.

495
00:32:14.852 --> 00:32:16.204
Have I mentioned the restaurant?

496
00:32:16.228 --> 00:32:18.814
Prince of Monaco eats
there every other week.

497
00:32:19.690 --> 00:32:20.730
Then I hope you're paying.

498
00:32:26.947 --> 00:32:30.492
I know I don't need to say it
again. but you deserve to hear it.

499
00:32:32.286 --> 00:32:35.372
What you did. I'll never forget it.

500
00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:41.670
Anything you ever
need from me. any favor.

501
00:32:43.297 --> 00:32:44.339
it's yours.

502
00:32:51.597 --> 00:32:53.432
Long way to come for a cigar.

503
00:32:56.393 --> 00:32:59.813
I'm told you haven't lived until you've
smoked a cigar in hôtel lumineux.

504
00:33:02.524 --> 00:33:04.151
- Hey.
- Hey.

505
00:33:06.486 --> 00:33:10.091
- You're not surprised to see me.
- No. I'm not.

506
00:33:10.115 --> 00:33:12.343
For someone who claims
not to have anything to do with

507
00:33:12.367 --> 00:33:13.368
your father's business.

508
00:33:14.828 --> 00:33:16.830
you certainly seem to be involved.

509
00:33:18.749 --> 00:33:20.894
I told you. the only way this ends well

510
00:33:20.918 --> 00:33:22.920
is if you let your husband go.

511
00:33:23.587 --> 00:33:26.024
My husband is not to blame here.

512
00:33:26.048 --> 00:33:28.800
He has five million dollars
of my family's money.

513
00:33:29.426 --> 00:33:31.654
Your family killed his wife.

514
00:33:31.678 --> 00:33:35.408
I know he believes that. but
there is simply no basis for it.

515
00:33:35.432 --> 00:33:37.911
Did you know Kate
spoke with a us attorney

516
00:33:37.935 --> 00:33:41.164
about Nicholas's work with
your dad just before she died?

517
00:33:41.188 --> 00:33:42.499
Yes.

518
00:33:42.523 --> 00:33:43.583
Bailey told me that.

519
00:33:43.607 --> 00:33:47.378
And I told her that she is looking
for answers where there are none.

520
00:33:47.402 --> 00:33:49.488
Right. You've been
completely transparent with her.

521
00:33:50.113 --> 00:33:52.032
I've made real efforts with Bailey.

522
00:33:53.283 --> 00:33:56.703
If my brother killed her
mother. I'd make real efforts too.

523
00:33:57.204 --> 00:34:00.391
Teddy didn't have the brains
or the wherewithal back then

524
00:34:00.415 --> 00:34:03.394
to do anything even remotely like this.

525
00:34:03.418 --> 00:34:05.063
I don't know.

526
00:34:05.087 --> 00:34:07.148
He's pretty good at making a mess.

527
00:34:07.172 --> 00:34:11.236
Kate was my friend. and it
was a difficult thing to get past.

528
00:34:11.260 --> 00:34:13.863
but this has nothing to
do with the matter at hand.

529
00:34:13.887 --> 00:34:15.405
But doesn't it?

530
00:34:15.429 --> 00:34:18.117
Everything. It all
started with Kate's death.

